WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.460
Is a mealworm a worm?

2
00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:03.660
It looks like one.

3
00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:08.200
But keep a few in a tub for some weeks, and something else climbs out.

4
00:00:11.233 --> 00:00:13.573
A kitten looks like a small cat from birth.

5
00:00:14.793 --> 00:00:16.533
A mealworm changes into a beetle.

6
00:00:17.853 --> 00:00:21.033
At each visit, your child counts and records what they see.

7
00:00:22.313 --> 00:00:24.173
Over time, they can check what changed.

8
00:00:25.233 --> 00:00:30.393
You need ten to twenty ordinary mealworms from a bait shop or pet store, not giant

9
00:00:30.393 --> 00:00:36.853
ones. Add a clear plastic tub with a lid, rolled oats or wheat bran, and a carrot or

10
00:00:36.853 --> 00:00:37.853
potato.

11
00:00:38.317 --> 00:00:41.117
Stay with your child whenever the tub is open.

12
00:00:42.397 --> 00:00:43.897
Keep the lid on between visits.

13
00:00:45.237 --> 00:00:49.717
Keep insects, bedding, and vegetable slices away from children under four.

14
00:00:50.977 --> 00:00:53.057
Call nine one one if a child is choking.

15
00:00:54.397 --> 00:00:55.877
Keep everything out of mouths.

16
00:00:57.177 --> 00:00:59.137
Wash hands with soap after each visit.

17
00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:05.267
If your child has asthma or a shellfish or dust mite allergy, ask their doctor

18
00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:10.347
first. For wheat allergy, use only bedding their allergist approves.

19
00:01:12.027 --> 00:01:15.567
Skip if in doubt. Open the tub away from faces.

20
00:01:16.867 --> 00:01:18.967
If breathing is hard, call nine one one.

21
00:01:20.217 --> 00:01:23.517
With the lid flat, poke ten to twenty small air holes.

22
00:01:24.757 --> 00:01:27.437
Add oats or bran three to five centimeters deep.

23
00:01:28.637 --> 00:01:31.597
Cut two thin carrot slices and lay them on top.

24
00:01:32.877 --> 00:01:33.877
They provide water.

25
00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:36.740
Tip the mealworms onto a plate.

26
00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:40.180
Use a hand lens to count legs together.

27
00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.380
Ask, 'What do you think it will turn into?'

28
00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:47.500
Record the guess. Measure two or three mealworms.

29
00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:50.700
Then spoon all the mealworms into the tub.

30
00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:54.910
Keep the tub at room temperature and out of direct sun.

31
00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:57.890
Visit two or three times a week.

32
00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:00.210
Look for shed skins.

33
00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:02.870
Count and record each stage.

34
00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:06.370
Replace the carrot every two or three days.

35
00:02:07.483 --> 00:02:10.443
The first pupae often appear within a few weeks.

36
00:02:11.723 --> 00:02:13.703
A pupa is pale, curled, and still.

37
00:02:15.043 --> 00:02:18.463
Use a soft brush to move it to a small dish with a little bran.

38
00:02:19.643 --> 00:02:22.003
This keeps the other insects from chewing on it.

39
00:02:22.917 --> 00:02:25.017
Picture the pale pupa in its dish.

40
00:02:26.257 --> 00:02:29.777
Your child sees it sitting still and wonders what will happen next.

41
00:02:30.837 --> 00:02:32.117
What do you think will come out?

42
00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:41.760
After about one to three weeks as a pupa, a pale beetle comes out.

43
00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:45.560
Once it darkens, move it back into the main tub.

44
00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:48.260
Check the first guess together.

45
00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:52.780
Measure the beetle and compare it with your mealworm measurements.

46
00:02:53.867 --> 00:02:57.067
Look for tiny mealworms in the bedding after a few weeks.

47
00:02:58.427 --> 00:03:02.567
Draw the four stages together: egg, larva, pupa, and adult beetle.

48
00:03:04.007 --> 00:03:07.907
Ask, 'Which looks like its parent from the start, a kitten or a mealworm?'

49
00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:11.110
Make a plan with your child at the start.

50
00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:14.170
Never release the insects outdoors.

51
00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:17.290
Offer them to an animal keeper.

52
00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:23.330
If nobody takes them, an adult chills them in a sealed container in the fridge for a

53
00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:29.010
few hours. Then the adult freezes them in a sealed bag for at least three days

54
00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:30.010
before disposal.

55
00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:33.513
Look back at the drawing and the notes together.

56
00:03:34.893 --> 00:03:37.233
Ask, 'What changed before the beetle came out?'

57
00:03:37.713 --> 00:03:39.253
Your child can point to what they saw.
